The strict rule survives serialization because `max_shortfall_pct` carries NO
omitempty (internal/models/spending_optimizer.go, struct read directly) while
the WhatIfSettings field is `*SpendingSearchPreferences ... omitempty` -- a
non-nil pointer to a zero struct still serializes. Verified at the file level
live: a blank-advanced Apply wrote exactly {"max_shortfall_pct": 12.5} with the
four omitempty fields absent (see (e)).
=> (b) MET.

